WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.749
After many days of summer, the riverbank was busy.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.557
Rat watched the birds packing their nests.

3
00:00:08.558 --> 00:00:12.682
"Why do they have to fly south?" thought Rat.

4
00:00:12.683 --> 00:00:16.893
"The riverbank is perfectly fine."

5
00:00:16.894 --> 00:00:20.599
"Hey, Ratty!" called some mice.

6
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.292
"Come and help."

7
00:00:22.293 --> 00:00:26.624
They walked by carrying baskets and boxes.

8
00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:29.616
"What are you up to?" asked Rat.

9
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:34.633
"Moving! To our winter home," said one mouse.

10
00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:38.054
"But it's a beautiful day," said Rat.

11
00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:40.580
"Winter is far away."

12
00:00:40.581 --> 00:00:44.599
"Oh, we know that," said another mouse.

13
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.605
"But we like to be ready!"

14
00:00:47.606 --> 00:00:50.704
"Let's go for a row," said Rat.

15
00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:52.913
"We can have a picnic!"

16
00:00:52.914 --> 00:00:56.001
"Not today, Rat!" said the first mouse.

17
00:00:56.002 --> 00:01:00.419
"Ask another day, when no one is busy."

18
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.276
Rat frowned. "Fine! Do what you want!"

19
00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:09.090
He turned and tripped over a box.

20
00:01:09.091 --> 00:01:13.340
"Ow!" cried Rat, rubbing his back.

21
00:01:13.341 --> 00:01:17.642
"Be more careful," said a bluebird.

22
00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.776
"Be quiet," said Rat.

23
00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:22.132
"I don't need any advice."

24
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.494
Birds flew around Rat's head.

25
00:01:25.495 --> 00:01:28.663
"What's the hurry?" Rat yelled at them.

26
00:01:28.664 --> 00:01:31.557
"We're not going yet," said a robin.

27
00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:34.001
"But we will!"

28
00:01:34.002 --> 00:01:37.477
"Why don't you stay this year?" asked Rat.

29
00:01:37.478 --> 00:01:39.685
"You always like it here."

30
00:01:39.686 --> 00:01:42.732
"We have to go," said the bluebird.

31
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:45.994
"The south calls us!"

32
00:01:45.995 --> 00:01:50.422
Before long, the mice and the birds were off.

33
00:01:50.423 --> 00:01:54.063
Rat heard footsteps and turned around.

34
00:01:54.064 --> 00:01:57.305
A visitor stood in the road.

35
00:01:57.306 --> 00:02:02.722
It was a dusty rat in a sailor's cap.

